      "side": 1,
      "message": "The whole problem is that when we plug wired headphones we set A2DP as inactive (we set a2dp active device to null) so it disappears in the audio framework - and since it\u0027s still connected it should be feasible to select from the audio framework point of view. Check Eric\u0027s comment on the bug: https://buganizer.corp.google.com/issues/202832397#comment22\n\nThe initial cause for all this wired device handling implemenation was that it wasn\u0027t possible to select back BT device when wired connected - and it\u0027s not the case anymore. It\u0027s unfeasible to check the underlying issue because the bugreports from the initial case are deleted, the bug is from 2018 ; )\n\nI did some testing:\nI removed wired handling and checked some scenarios - two bt devices and one wired, plugged/unplugged and tested if it plays on the correct device. Both for LE Audio and A2DP. \nAnother test that I did was a phone call and plugging/unplugging wired - it selects a proper device and everything works. \n\nI think it\u0027s safe to try and remove it under the flag.",
